WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
It starts on one small island.

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.430
Then ships carry English
across the oceans,

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.810
to North America and Australia.

4
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.910
Then to India, Nigeria and Singapore.

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.080
Then planes, screens and the
internet carry it everywhere.

6
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.880
Today, most English speakers
aren't native speakers at all.

7
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.720
So whose English is it?

8
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.750
In this mission, you'll
trace how English spread,

9
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.770
in three big phases.

10
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.050
You'll sort the world's users into rings,

11
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.030
from the centre outwards.

12
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.750
And you'll meet new Englishes,
and ask: are they mistakes,

13
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.570
or rules of their own?

14
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: decide whose
English it really is.
